MayteraOS userland libc - MIT License
======================================

This directory (userland/libc/) is MayteraOS's freestanding C library for
Ring 3 user-mode applications. It is deliberately licensed under the
permissive MIT License below, NOT under the GPLv2-or-later license that
covers the MayteraOS kernel and OS source (see LICENSE / COPYING at the
repository root).

Why: every ported or first-party userland application statically links
userland/libc/libc.a. A copyleft license on libc would impose GPL terms
on every application linked against it, which would exclude a large
class of permissively- and Apache-licensed software from ever being
ported to MayteraOS on a technicality about the library, not about the
application. A permissive libc is infrastructure, not the product; this
is the same reasoning behind musl (MIT) and newlib (BSD) in other
freestanding/embedded C library projects. See
docs/PORTABILITY_HOMEBREW_SNAPCRAFT_ASSESSMENT.md section 7.2 for the
full analysis that led to this decision.

Scope: this license covers userland/libc/ only (every .c and .h file
under this directory carries a short "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT"
header pointing back to this file). It does not apply to the kernel, to
other userland applications, or to vendored third-party components
elsewhere in the tree; see ATTRIBUTION.md at the repository root for the
complete per-component license table.

